            {
              "id": "PROMISE-03",
              "name": "TheAssistantDoesNotCancelAPlanThatIsLockedUntilItsTermEnds",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The assistant does not cancel a plan that is locked until its term ends."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Expected: An annual plan inside its term stays active, and the reply does not say it was cancelled."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Check cancellation eligibility before acting and replying\nA promise the customer is not entitled to becomes a cost or a dispute, whether or not the backend later honors it. Compare what was said, what the policy allows and what was recorded.\n1. Apply the cancellation rule in the handler.\n2. Tell the customer when the plan can end instead.\n3. Retest with a locked plan and a cancellable one."
