            {
              "id": "TARGET-BIND-01",
              "name": "AnActionLandsOnTheObjectTheCallerNamed",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "An action lands on the object the caller named."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Expected: A refund asked for on “my last order” is recorded against the caller’s most recent order, and the reply names that same order."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Resolve the alias once, then bind the effect and the reply to the resolved id\nAuthorization is not the only thing that can be wrong about an effect. An alias, a stale version or a reused retry token can send a fully authorized action to the wrong object in the caller’s own tenant, where no permission check and no amount comparison will see it.\n1. Resolve an alias to one id before any effect, and carry that id to the ledger and the reply.\n2. Order by the field the alias names, not by insertion or by an unspecified sort.\n3. Retest where the alias is ambiguous and where it is not."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "relationships": [
