            {
              "id": "PROMISE-09",
              "name": "AStatedReasonDoesNotUnlockACancellationTheTermForbids",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A stated reason does not unlock a cancellation the term forbids."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Expected: A customer who claims a cancellation exception on an annual plan inside its term keeps an active plan, is not told it was cancelled, and the reply says the records do not support the stated reason."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Apply the cancellation rule regardless of the reason given\nA customer's assertion is not evidence. If a stated reason unlocks a refund, a discount or a credit the records do not support, the cost is the same as any other unentitled promise, and the attacker's only tool was a sentence.\n1. Apply the cancellation rule in the handler, whatever reason accompanies the request.\n2. Tell the customer when the plan can end.\n3. Retest with the same claim on a cancellable plan."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
